From 0fb4009b44276c2ed87268ab48053c5942b69ca5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John R Reeves III <johnreevesiii@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:49:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] linkbus: vblank barrier; loud snapshot failures (review
 C1, C2, F4, F5, F11)

C1: frame sync at retro_run return did not keep the boards' guest time
equal: a retro_run ends at a rendered frame or the render timeout, so
the master ran about 1.8 vblanks per round and the satellites about 1.
linkbus_install_vblank_barrier adds a VBlank listener (installed before
the comm board's) that stores the board's vblank count in the mailbox
(MailboxLayout::vblankCount) and waits until the hub has published that
round (MailboxLayout::hubRound), bounded by a timeout; barrierStop
releases it at shutdown. The hub publishes round k once every seat has
reached vblank k, after delivering each seat's newest slot frame, so
every seat advances exactly one guest vblank per round, as natively
(one hub tick per vblank), and the comm board's take at vblank k reads
every seat's vblank k - 1 publish.

C2: a first or second multiboard barrier timeout, a vblank barrier
timeout and a snapshot sync index mismatch are counted, logged once and
latch a nondeterministic flag. The snapshot log header now carries the
sync index, checked against the peer's before applying.
linkbus_mb_stats (10 u32) replaces linkbus_sab_snapshot_stats.

F4: status ops fold into one AND mask and one OR mask per sync, so the
log holds at most one entry per word and cannot overflow (logEntries is
kMbDataWords). F5: a peer's log count is clamped to the region. F11:
the destructor clears the stats pointer.

